    <description>A large, hard-shelled mite that nests in the fuel bunkers of wrecked ships and has adapted to live on the residue. Sacs beneath its shell concentrate that residue into raw chemfuel, which a threatened fethrik sprays in a wide cone. The fuel coats whatever it hits without catching fire. Fethriks are restless, short-lived and quick to breed.</description>
